                "table": 1,
                "text": "(in billions, except for percentages) | Q425 | FY25 | Q126 | Q226 | Q326 | Q426 | FY26\nCommercial (Includes commercial portion of LinkedIn) Commercial (Includes commercial portion of LinkedIn) |  |  |  |  |  |  | \nCommercial bookings growth (y/y)* For commercial products and cloud services, sum of revenue growth, plus change in balance of unearned revenue plus the change in contracted not billed balance | 37% / 30% | 38% | 112% / 111% | 230% / 228% | -4% / -6% | 10% / 11% | 83%\nCommercial remaining performance obligation Commercial portion of revenue allocated to remaining performance obligations, which includes unearned revenue and amounts that will be invoiced and recognized as revenue in future periods | $368 | $368 | $392 | $625 | $627 | $678 | $678\nMicrosoft Cloud revenue Revenue from Microsoft 365 Commercial cloud, Azure and other cloud services, the commercial portion of LinkedIn, and Dynamics 365 | $46.7 | $168.9 | $49.1 | $51.5 | $54.5 | $59.3 | $214.4\nMicrosoft Cloud revenue growth (y/y)* Revenue from Microsoft 365 Commercial cloud, Azure and other cloud services, the commercial portion of LinkedIn, and Dynamics 365 | 27% / 25% | 23% / 23% | 26% / 25% | 26% / 24% | 29% / 25% | 27% / 27% | 27% / 25%\nMicrosoft Cloud gross margin percentage Gross margin percentage for our Microsoft Cloud business | 68% | 69% | 68% | 67% | 66% | 65% | 66%\nProductivity & Business Processes and Intelligent Cloud Productivity & Business Processes and Intelligent Cloud |  |  |  |  |  |  | \nMicrosoft 365 Commercial cloud revenue growth (y/y)* Revenue from Microsoft 365 Commercial subscriptions, comprising Microsoft 365 Commercial, Enterprise Mobility + Security, the cloud portion of Windows Commercial, the per-user portion of Power BI, Exchange, SharePoint, Microsoft Teams, Microsoft 365 Security and Compliance, and Microsoft 365 Copilot | 18% / 16% | 15% / 15% | 17% / 15% | 17% / 14% | 19% / 15% | 14% / 14% | 17% / 14%\nMicrosoft 365 Commercial seat growth (y/y) Microsoft 365 Commercial seat growth: the number of Microsoft 365 Commercial seats at end of period where seats are paid users covered by a Microsoft 365 Commercial subscription | 6% | 6% | 6% | 6% | 6% | 6% | 6%\nMicrosoft 365 Consumer cloud revenue growth (y/y)* Revenue from Microsoft 365 Consumer subscriptions and other consumer services | 20% / 20% | 11% / 12% | 26% / 25% | 29% / 27% | 33% / 29% | 24% / 22% | 28% / 26%\nLinkedIn revenue growth (y/y)* Revenue from LinkedIn, including Talent Solutions, Marketing Solutions, Premium Subscriptions, and Sales Solutions | 9% / 8% | 9% / 9% | 10%/ 9% | 11% / 10% | 12% / 9% | 12% / 10% | 11% / 9%\nDynamics 365 revenue growth (y/y)* Revenue from Dynamics 365, including a set of intelligent, cloud-based applications across ERP, CRM, Power Apps, and Power Automate | 23% / 21% | 19% / 19% | 18% / 16% | 19% / 17% | 22% / 17% | 13% / 12% | 18% / 15%\nAzure and other cloud services revenue growth (y/y)* Revenue from Azure and other cloud services, including cloud and AI consumption-based services, GitHub cloud services, Nuance Healthcare cloud services, virtual desktop offerings, and other cloud services | 39% / 39% | 34% / 35% | 40% / 39% | 39% / 38% | 40% / 39% | 43% / 43% | 41% / 40%\nMore Personal Computing More Personal Computing |  |  |  |  |  |  | \nWindows OEM and Devices revenue growth (y/y)* Revenue from sales of Windows Pro and non-Pro licenses sold through the OEM channel and sales of first-party Devices, including Surface and PC accessories | 3% / 3% | 3% / 3% | 6% / 6% | 1% / 0% | -2% / -3% | -7% / -7% | -1% / -1%\nXBOX content and services revenue growth (y/y)* Revenue from XBOX content and services, comprising first- and third-party content (including games and in-game content), XBOX Game Pass and other subscriptions, XBOX Cloud Gaming, advertising, and other cloud services | 13% / 12% | 16% / 16% | 1% / 0% | -5% / -6% | -5% / -7% | -10% / -10% | -5% / -6%\nSearch advertising revenue (ex TAC) growth (y/y)* Revenue from search advertising excluding traffic acquisition costs (\"TAC\") paid to Bing Ads network publishers and content partners | 21% / 20% | 20% / 21% | 16% / 15% | 10% / 9% | 12% / 9% | 10% / 9% | 12% / 10%"
